[P078_ROUTER_FIRST_ANSWER_SAMPLE] {"policy": "constant_train_mean", "case": 0, "action": 2, "first_answer": {"input_text": "<|im_start|>user\nGive a concise answer to the question using only the reference.\nQuestion:\nWhen did a district court order the FDA to stop approving antibiotics in animals?\nReference:\nThere has been extensive use of antibiotics in animal husbandry. In the United States, the question of emergence of antibiotic-resistant bacterial strains due to use of antibiotics in livestock was raised by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) in 1977. In March 2012, the United States District Court for the Southern District of New York, ruling in an action brought by the Natural Resources Defense Council and others, ordered the FDA to revoke approvals for the use of antibiotics in livestock, which violated FDA regulations.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n", "prefix_ids": [3, 26791, 233, 73, 567, 295, 4317, 1318, 5315, 337, 299, 3538, 1901, 1278, 299, 7164, 48, 233, 10922, 17552, 60, 233, 3745, 2092, 295, 10590, 6378, 2566, 299, 16789, 337, 4222, 2245, 2124, 13859, 329, 3940, 65, 233, 15256, 3376, 60, 233, 3184, 831, 1091, 10216, 1165, 322, 13859, 329, 4933, 12598, 878, 48, 788, 299, 2591, 2749, 46, 299, 3538, 322, 23165, 322, 19932, 47, 23942, 15571, 19546, 3058, 337, 1165, 322, 13859, 329, 17780, 610, 8697, 585, 299, 2840, 7393, 334, 15705, 13158, 406, 72, 6664, 43, 329, 8585, 48, 788, 5303, 2669, 46, 299, 2591, 2749, 12730, 8380, 432, 299, 10573, 12730, 322, 1895, 3703, 46, 20009, 329, 488, 4209, 5580, 585, 299, 10784, 12532, 20589, 6764, 334, 2748, 46, 12954, 299, 16789, 337, 4398, 5521, 2245, 20657, 432, 299, 1165, 322, 13859, 329, 17780, 46, 773, 4406, 720, 16789, 11024, 48, 4, 233, 3, 917, 14491, 233], "actual_answer": "The question of emergence of antibiotic-resistant bacterial strains due to use of antibiotics in livestock is a complex question. In the United States, the question of emergence of antibiotic-resistant bacterial strains due to u